# Design: `FormedCore`, a minimal-interface module for what the Core holds while formed

Scope of reading: I read CoreBlockEntity.java, DoorwayHandlers.java, the call sites in CoreMenu, PlanterMenu and JadeInfo, MeLink, and ADRs 0005, 0006 and 0009 plus GLOSSARY.md. I did NOT read PowerPool, FertilizerPool, OutputSink, LiveBlocks, MPBlockEntities beyond the capability registration lines (46-48), or the GameTests beyond grep hits. Pool method names below (stored, capacity, available, fillPercent) come from existing call sites. I did not run `entire graph` or `entire brain`. The design is unverified against those classes.

## 1. Interface

`FormedCore` is immutable and lives in `J/multiblock/`. It has two states, running and paused. CoreBlockEntity swaps the instance rather than mutating it, and holds one `@Nullable FormedCore formed` field in place of the six.

```java
public final class FormedCore {
  // Builds the pools, finds the ME link, builds the Doorway handlers. Call only when all parts are loaded.
  public static FormedCore running(Level level, Multiblock mb, Runnable onStale);
  // Keeps the Multiblock, holds no pools and no ME link (ADR 0009).
  public static FormedCore paused(Multiblock mb);

  // 1. Ticks every planter in Multiblock order. No-op when paused or when any part is unloaded.
  public void tick(ServerLevel level, long phase);

  // 2. Totals plus planter positions for the Core screen. Zeros and NONE when paused.
  public Totals totals();
  public record Totals(List<BlockPos> planters, long energyStored, long energyCapacity,
                       int fertilizer, int outputFillPercent, MeStatus me) {
    public static final Totals EMPTY = /* empty list, zeros, MeStatus.NONE */;
  }

  // 3. The only remote-open authorization. False when paused.
  public boolean owns(BlockPos planter);

  // 4. Doorway for pipes. Null when paused.
  public @Nullable Doorway doorway();
  public record Doorway(EnergyHandler energy, ResourceHandler<ItemResource> items) {}
}
```

This is four entry points, one over the budget. `owns` is the one I would not drop. Folding it into `totals()` would push the authorization back into callers and make `stillValid` compute sums every tick. The `planters` list in `Totals` includes the kept planters while paused, because the Core screen shows loaded planter rows during a wait today.

Invariants, ordering and error modes:
- `phase` is `gameTime + core.tickOffset()`. The ME interval check is `phase % ME_INTERVAL == 0`.
- `onStale` fires when a pool or the ME link reports a removed member. It fires from `tick`, `totals` or a handler call, never from the factory. CoreBlockEntity points it at `markPoolsStale`, so the next scan rebuilds.
- No method throws. Absent pools mean zeros, `false`, `null` or a no-op.
- ME calls happen only inside `tick`, never inside Doorway handlers, so no transaction is open during an ME call. The `MeLink` contract is unchanged.
- `owns` is true only when running and the Multiblock's `planters()` contains the position. Server-side only. The client never gets this object.

## 2. Usage

```java
// CoreBlockEntity.tickPlanters
if (formed != null && level instanceof ServerLevel sl)
  formed.tick(sl, sl.getGameTime() + tickOffset());

// CoreMenu.buildTable
FormedCore.Totals t = core.formed() == null ? Totals.EMPTY : core.formed().totals();
for (BlockPos pos : t.planters()) { /* isLoaded + PlanterBlockEntity rows, draw */ }
new CoreTablePayload.Totals(scan.formed(), scan.partCount(), cap, scan.problem(),
    Optional.ofNullable(scan.problemPos()), t.energyStored(), t.energyCapacity(), draw,
    t.fertilizer(), t.outputFillPercent(), t.me());

// Remote open: CoreMenu.openPlanter and PlanterMenu.stillInCoreStructure both reduce to
core.formed() != null && core.formed().owns(pos)
```

## 3. What the implementation hides

- The three pools, the nullable `MeLink`, and the `LiveBlocks` stale callbacks.
- `onlineMe()` and removed-link handling: a removed link counts as absent and fires the stale callback.
- `power.refillFrom`, the `TickContext` construction (`AteBridge.numbers()`, `fertilizer.budget()`, outputs), and the planter loop.
- The ME_INTERVAL transfers (`moveExportsInto`, `topUpFrom`).
- The `blockEntities(level, positions, type)` collection helper.
- The all-parts-loaded check (`multiblock.all()` against `level::isLoaded`), which leaves CoreBlockEntity's public surface.
- The combined item handler (`CombinedResourceHandler` plus the `DelegatingResourceHandler` fallback when a member is not live).
- The paused versus running distinction, which callers see only as zeros, `false`, `null` or a no-op.

## 4. Dependency strategy

- Pools, `Multiblock` and the handlers are in-process.
- `MeLink` is the existing seam with two adapters: the `ae2` package adapter and the fake `MeLink` used in tests (ADR 0005). It is real, and unchanged.
- `FormedCore` has one implementation and no interface. A second adapter would be hypothetical, so no seam is added (project rule: repetition beats premature abstraction).
- The world (`Level`, block entities) is true-external. The module touches it only through the `Level` passed to `running` and `tick`. JadeInfo stays Jade-free because it uses `lastScan()` only.

## 5. Trade-offs

Leverage is high:
- `totals()` replaces the four null checks in `buildTable`.
- `owns` replaces the double check (`multiblock != null && lastScan().formed()`) in two places. Paused implies not owned, so the `lastScan().formed()` check is no longer needed. This preserves behaviour because a kept Multiblock with a non-WAITING scan is formed by construction.
- Locality: stale or removed-member bugs concentrate in `FormedCore`.

Leverage is thin:
- `Doorway` is a two-field record and `tick` has one caller. `tick` earns its place by hiding, not by reuse.
- Four entry points is one over budget.

CoreBlockEntity surface after the change:

| Accessor | Fate |
|---|---|
| `lastScan()` | Kept (Jade, Core screen, GameTests) |
| `markDirty()` | Kept (CoreFinder) |
| `serverTick` | Kept |
| `formed()` | New, returns `@Nullable FormedCore` |
| `tickOffset()` | Made private, since `phase` is passed in |
| `multiblock()` | Removed. GameTests use `formed().totals().planters()` or a Multiblock getter on the module |
| `power()` | Removed. Replaced by `totals().energyStored()` and `energyCapacity()` |
| `fertilizer()` | Removed. Replaced by `totals().fertilizer()` |
| `outputs()` | Removed. See GameTest costs below |
| `items()` | Removed. Replaced by `doorway().items()` |
| `meStatus()` | Removed. Replaced by `totals().me()` |
| `allPartsLoaded()` | Removed (only Core used it, per rg) |

GameTest costs:
- StructureTests: mechanical (`multiblock()` becomes `formed()`).
- CoreScreenTests: `outputs() != null` becomes `formed() != null`.
- Ae2Tests: it calls `outputs().insert(...)` and `outputs().hasRoomFor(...)`, and `doorway().items()` is extract-only. This is not purely mechanical. It needs a decision from the owner: either a package-private test hook on `FormedCore`, or inserting through a different route. This is the one open point.

DoorwayHandlers is deleted. Its `energy(core)` and `items(core)` pass-throughs fail the deletion test, so no complexity reappears. The `items(fertilizer, outputs)` builder moves into `FormedCore` as a private method. The MPBlockEntities capability lambdas (lines 46-48) become `be.formed() == null ? null : (doorway == null ? null : doorway.energy())` and the same for `items`. `level.invalidateCapabilities(worldPosition)` stays in `scan()` after the instance swap.

Behaviour caveat: a paused `totals()` returns zeros, not last known values. This matches today, where the pools are null while waiting.

