Called the Read tool with the following input: {"file_path":"/Users/sweetjp/DEV/git_repos/minecraft-mods/ModularPlanters/docs/agents/minecraft-lookups.md"}
Result of calling the Read tool:
1	# Minecraft, NeoForge and addon lookups
2	
3	Check every class, method, registry id and version against the `minecraft-modding` MCP server (`@adhisang/minecraft-modding-mcp`, run through `bunx`) before writing it. `.mcp.json` is gitignored, so add the server to your own client first.
4	
5	The `target` decides whether a class is found:
6	
7	| To read                                       | Target                                                                                             |
8	| --------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
9	| Vanilla                                       | `{kind: version, value: <minecraft_version>}`                                                      |
10	| NeoForge source                               | `{kind: dependency, group: net.neoforged, name: neoforge, version: <neo_version>}`                 |
11	| NeoForge members, or a source read that fails | `{kind: jar, value: <neoforge-<version>-universal.jar>}`, found under `~/.gradle/caches/modules-2` |
12	| FML, such as `ModList`                        | `jar` target on `net.neoforged.fancymodloader:loader` at the version in the NeoForge pom           |
13	| AE2 and other addons                          | `jar` target on the addon's jar under `~/.gradle/caches/modules-2`                                 |
14	
15	- Pass explicit versions. `versionFromProject` reads `neoforge_version` and ignores `neo_version`, so `gradle.properties` carries both with the same value. Change them together.
16	- `workspace` targets miss NeoForge and FML classes, because the patched jars in `build/moddev/artifacts` do not contain them.
17	- Say what could not be verified when a lookup fails and the answer matters.
18	

